+## Session expiry
+
+Each saved session is stamped with an `issued_at` timestamp (epoch seconds). A session older
+than `SESSION_TTL` (3600 seconds) is rejected on restore with `SessionExpiredError`; a missing,
+malformed, or future `issued_at` is also rejected. `purge_expired()` removes expired entries from
+the on-disk cache and is called at the start of every `load_session`.
+
+The resume blob is base64 of JSON: `{"issued_at": <epoch seconds>, "session": {...}}`. Pickle is
+no longer used. Note that `issued_at` is client-supplied, so sign the blob (e.g. HMAC) if clients
+are untrusted.
